  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 14</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ealle Godes gerihta fyrðrige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ ealle Godes gerihta friðige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14" corresp="#wit-q">Et omnes rectitudines et sanctę Dei cerimonię, sicut omnibus opus est, totis desideriis obseruentur</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="14" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ealle Godes gerihta fyrðrige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ealle Godes gerihta fyrðrige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">And all God's dues shall be promptly rendered, as the occasion requires.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And all God’s dues are to be given willingly, just as is required.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und alle Kirchengerechtsame fördere (schütze A) man willig, wie es nöthig ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let all God's dues be eagerly promoted (protected, A), as is needful.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="295"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_21-1">VI Atr 21.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 21, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 21.1.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">fyrðrige: friðige A</note>
      </div>
    </body>
